 2. Aaaaand action! 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo: Samuel Boivin/NurPhoto via Getty Image

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Paramount Skydance agreed to a highly anticipated settlement today with 12 state attorneys general who sued to block its $110 billion acquisition of Warner Bros. Discovery, the company confirmed in a filing.

 🎬 Why it matters: The settlement clears the path for the creation of one of the biggest TV and movie behemoths in the world and ends what has been one of the most expensive, drawn-out and dramatic merger fights in U.S. history, Axios' Sara Fischer reports .

 🔍 Zoom in: As part of the settlement, Paramount has agreed to make a series of behavioral concessions — in the areas of film distribution, production and more — in exchange for not having to divest key assets, including WBD's lucrative cable networks.

